SUMMARY:Oakville Waterfront Walk\, Talk and Social! (September 20th) 
DESCRIPTION:Soul City Social Club (Toronto\, Canada)\n\\*\\*\\*Please kind
 ly read carefully\\*\\*\\*\n\nHello everyone\,\n\nCome join us for a beaut
 iful and relaxing afternoon by the lake as Soul City Social Club heads to 
 **Oakville for a Waterfront Walk\, Talk and Social!**\n\nWe’ll meet near
  the Oakville waterfront and begin with a few fun and easy ice-breaker gam
 es to help everyone get introduced and comfortable. From there\, we’ll h
 ead out for a leisurely walk along the waterfront\, enjoying the harbour\,
  Lake Ontario\, parks and some of the beautiful scenery Oakville has to of
 fer.\n\nThis is a social\, leisure walk. We’ll keep a comfortable pace\,
  stop along the way\, mix up the group and give everyone plenty of opportu
 nities to meet and talk with different people.\n\nThe area also has plenty
  of cafés\, restaurants and boutiques to explore\, along with beautiful t
 ree-lined streets and impressive heritage homes that add to the charm of t
 he walk.\n\nJoined by my other groups too\; so we can antiicapte a wonderf
 ul day!\n\n\\*Many of us will most likely hit a near by pub as well for di
 nner and beverages after\n\n**Location and When to Meet:**\n\\*We will mee
 t outfront Tim Hortons (49 Lakeshore Rd. W) at 4:00 pm-and wait for everyo
 ne until 4:30 pm (please arrive on time)\n\nMore Details below:\n\nSincere
 ly\,\n\nSteve Flemming\n(Organizer/Host)\n\nDetails here:\n\n**Oakville Wa
 terfront Walk\, Talk and Social!**\n\n• A few fun ice-breaker games near
  the beginning to get everyone talking and laughing\n• A leisurely water
 front walk with plenty of time to socialize\n• Beautiful views of Lake O
 ntario and the Oakville waterfront\n• A chance to meet new people and re
 connect with familiar faces\n• Stops along the way to relax\, chat and e
 njoy the surroundings\n• A friendly atmosphere welcoming friends\, singl
 es and couples\n• The possibility of grabbing a beverage and/or bite to 
 eat together afterward for anyone who wants to continue socializing\n\nWhe
 ther you’re coming on your own or bringing a friend\, the idea is simple
 : get outside\, enjoy the waterfront\, have some good conversations and sp
 end a few hours with some friendly people.\n\nNew members are always welco
 me\, and if you’re attending by yourself\, don’t worry—that’s exac
 tly why we’ll start with some ice-breakers and introductions.\nCome walk
 \, talk\, laugh and enjoy a little time by the lake!\n\n**Event Fee:**\n\n
 10 dollars (cash only) when you arrive (HST is included)\nor e transfer in
  advance to [Steveflemming11@gmail.com](mailto:Steveflemming11@gmail.com)\
 n\nLots of free park on Lakershore and surronding residential area\n\n**Wh
 ere to Find Us:**\n\\*We will meet right outfront the **Tim Hortons-** **4
 9 Lakeshore Rd. W-** Feel free to purchase a beverage when you arrive\n\\*
 Bathrooms provided there too\n\n**Coming from Toronto-Go Train:**\nOakvill
 e is easy to reach from Toronto by GO Train. Take the Lakeshore West line 
 from Union Station directly to Oakville GO Station\, with the trip taking 
 approximately 45–50 minutes.
